title: "NoiPhi: A stochastic noise simulation kit for quantum and photonic systems"
type: software
abstract: "NoiPhi is a Python package for generating physically realistic noise trajectories from experimental power spectral densities (PSDs), based on the Timmer-König (TK95) algorithm. It simulates laser phase and amplitude noise for quantum many-body and photonic systems."
version: 0.2.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.24474604
date-released: 2026-11-23
url: "https://github.com/SpeshalK/NoiPhi"
repository-code: "https://github.com/SpeshalK/NoiPhi"
keywords:
  - quantum noise simulation
  - laser noise
  - phase noise
  - amplitude noise
  - TK95 algorithm
  - photonics
